  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Mission Console",
    "overview": "EleSync is the console the user runs their AI crew from. Every assistant (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Grok and the rest) is a station reporting in, every project is a mission with its own boundary, and the dashboard is where the operator sees, at a glance, what is live, what is waiting, and what crossed a line. The room is dark on purpose. Deep indigo hulls recede so that the only things that light up are things worth reading: a status, an active project, a focused control, the elephant.\n\nThe console is **precise and quiet**. Density is real (12–14px working type, compact rows, mono numerals for counts), but nothing shouts. Borders are hairlines, corners are small, and surfaces sit flat as tonal layers. Light is a signal, not a decoration: violet means \"this is yours / this is selected\", cyan means \"this is live / this is telemetry\", and the green, amber and red status colours mean exactly what they say. The one place the console is allowed to perform is the active-project hero, where the elephant floats in its cyan-violet glow. It is the station's insignia, not wallpaper.\n\nThe UI is dark-only and treats the phone as a full console, not a port: the same mission state, compressed into a bottom tab bar and single-column panels, with real safe-area handling.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Dark-only indigo hull (`void` → `hull` → `hull-raised` → `hull-high`) with hairline `seam` borders.",
      "One accent (`signal-violet`) for ownership and selection; `telemetry-cyan` reserved for live state, info, focus rings and data.",
      "Geist for reading, Geist Mono for eyebrow labels and counts. Both are self-hosted and work offline.",
